Most code is from the MPlayer project.
- Bastiaan Stougie <wififreedom2026@protonmail.com>
  Sep. 2026:
  - option --detect-italic:
    Detect text that is italic and mark it as such in the output .srt file with
    <i> and </i> tags. Uses opencv contour detection to improve bounding boxes
    received from Tesseract, then looks at the leftmost symbol pixel in the top
    row and bottom row of the symbol bounding box to determine, based on
    collected statistics, if a symbol is italic or not. Propagates the results
    to the word and neighbouring words.
  - option --ocr-batch-size:
    Combine multiple subtitle images into one image for increased OCR accuracy
    and to prevent that OCR does not find any text if there's only a little
    text in a subtitle image.
  - options --base-duration and --chars-per-sec:
    limit maximum subtitle display information based on a bas duration plus
    a duration based on the characters per second a viewer reads.
  - options --debug-number and --debug-images:
    for debugging
  - fix for broken mplayer code that read past a buffer, causing an invalid
    palette and therefore broken images
  - fix for skipped subtitles: no longer look at start_pts, which caused
    skipped subtitle images if start_pts is the same
  - automatic threshold limit detection based on image color histogram
  - ability to sump subtitle images in any file format opencv supports
  - exception safety and exception handling
  - always replace "|" received from Tesseract with "I".
